# Secret group `monitor`: The public domain, the iOS app identifier for the Apple App Site
# Association file, and the dead-man monitor ping.
# Loaded by: alldots-dead-man.service, alldots-failping@.service.
#
# Ownership and mode are load-bearing: `root:root 0600`. systemd reads EnvironmentFile= as root
# before dropping privileges. provision.sh installs this template to
# /opt/alldots/shared/env/monitor.env only when that file does not exist, so an operator's values are
# never overwritten by a rerun, and it never prints a value. A key belongs to exactly one group
# (docs/architecture/delivery-and-operations.md); this file is excluded from restic backups.

# ALLDOTS_DOMAIN: the public Caddy domain, without a URL scheme. The dead-man timer probes
# https://$ALLDOTS_DOMAIN/healthz before it sends the monitor success ping.
ALLDOTS_DOMAIN=

# ALLDOTS_APPLE_TEAM_ID and ALLDOTS_IOS_BUNDLE_ID: from the Apple Developer account. Together they
# form the app identifier (<team id>.<bundle id>) in /.well-known/apple-app-site-association,
# which lets the iOS app open the password-reset link. provision.sh renders the file only when
# both are set; otherwise the path answers 404.
ALLDOTS_APPLE_TEAM_ID=
ALLDOTS_IOS_BUNDLE_ID=

# HEALTHCHECKS_PING_URL: pinged only after the five-minute dead-man timer's own public
# GET /healthz succeeds — this URL never substitutes for that check.
HEALTHCHECKS_PING_URL=
